## Project Structure

```
tryon_engine.py          # Main engine (all sections in one file)
garment.png              # Default garment image (replace with your own)
README.md                # This file
```

### Internal Sections

| Section | Contents |
|---|---|
| 1 | Configuration (`Config` class) |
| 2 | GPU helpers (OpenCV CUDA with CPU fallback) |
| 3 | EMA landmark smoother |
| 4 | Pose extractor (MediaPipe) |
| 5 | Body segmenter (MediaPipe) |
| 6 | Quad builder + drift limiter |
| 7 | Garment loader (alpha extraction) |
| 8 | Mesh warp engine |
| 9 | Torso suppression |
| 10 | Composite + arm occlusion |
| 11 | CatVTON diffusion engine |
| 12 | Garment preprocessor (rembg / fallback) |
| 13 | Main `TryOnPipeline` class |
| 14 | Node.js server bridge (stdin/stdout JSON) |
| 15 | Demo mode (webcam + OpenCV window) |

---

## Troubleshooting

**No pose detected**
The last warped overlay is shown as a ghost (18% opacity) until pose is re-acquired. Ensure adequate lighting and that shoulders are fully visible.

**Diffusion OOM error on 4GB GPU**
Reduce `DIFF_H` / `DIFF_W` in `Config` (e.g. 384×288) or lower `DIFF_STEPS` to 20.

**Slow live warp (CPU)**
Install OpenCV with CUDA support to enable GPU-accelerated blur, warp, and morphology operations.

**White garment background not removed**
Install `rembg` (`pip install rembg`) for accurate background removal. Without it, only simple white-threshold removal is used.

**xformers not found**
Install with `pip install xformers`. If unavailable, the engine still runs correctly using attention slicing + VAE tiling.

